content.text:
The second slice has reached its green implementation pass:

- the old `lost-101` lookup is gone;
- pending/unavailable coordinates defer before any model call;
- candidates must be active, within 30 days, within 15 verified-coordinate miles, and species-compatible;
- every eligible candidate is scored once, with score → distance → pet ID tie-breaking;
- the winner’s actual persisted breed/color/description feeds scoring—no injected Golden Retriever candidate traits remain.

The focused tests first failed on the old hard-coded/fallback behavior and now pass, including closed, expired, pending, out-of-radius, wrong-species, duplicate, concurrency, and browser-facing cascade cases.

